# check_tables.py thresholds — the manuscript-to-workbook binding.
#
# Copy the keys you want to a `.env` at your repo root (or up to three parents
# of the cwd). A real environment variable always beats the `.env` file.
# `python3 scripts/check_tables.py --list-checks` prints the values in force.
#
# The prefix used to be `SWS_`. That name is still read as a fallback, so an
# existing `.env` keeps working, but new keys should use `PAPERBELL_`.
#
# Defaults are measured, not invented — change them when the pipeline behaves
# differently, not to silence a finding.
#
# check_annotations.py has no thresholds on purpose: a mark is present or it is
# not.
#
# There is deliberately no threshold for "is this table big enough to deserve
# to exist". That is a judgement about the writing, and this pack owns encoding
# only.

# Words in a single row-1 cell before it is read as a caption rather than a
# column heading. Column headings are short by nature — "Swept range" is two
# words — so four separates them without a guess.
PAPERBELL_TABLE_CAPTION_MIN_WORDS=4

# The S-numbering block's position has no threshold on purpose: a long
# frontmatter is not a defect, so `si-s-prefix` asks whether a float precedes
# the block rather than which line it sits on.
